      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes profound sense that you feel there is no one left to perform your old roles for, especially when your entire identity was woven together with your care for her. The realization that your daily existence was tied so closely to her presence can feel like a death of the self, leaving you with no reason to keep the old routines going. This isn't necessarily a lack of hope, but often a crucial, difficult phase where your identity is in the process of being rewritten from within.",
